  "result": "`satisfies(version, range)` is now implemented in `src/semver.js` as specified in `docs/SPEC.md`, and `npm test` passes (10 of 10).\n\nThe tests are in `test/satisfies.test.js`. They cover every example table in the spec:\n- operators, partial versions and X-ranges\n- tilde, caret and hyphen ranges\n- prerelease ordering and the same-`MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH` rule\n- ignored build metadata\n- invalid versions and ranges returning `false`\n- very large integers\n- never throwing\n\nThe spec doesn't say what to do in these cases, so I chose:\n- **Wildcard then number:** a range like `1.x.3` is invalid and returns `false`.\n- **Partial with prerelease:** a range like `1.2-beta` is invalid and returns `false`.\n- **Prerelease leading zeros:** prerelease identifiers with leading zeros are accepted, since the spec only forbids them in `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`.\n- **Whitespace after `~` and `^`:** this is allowed, as it is for the comparison operators.\n- **`>*` and `<*`:** these match nothing.\n- **Invalid `||` set:** if any set in a `||` range is invalid, the whole range returns `false`, even when another set would match.\n\nI didn't call the advisor tool, because the task was small and the tests cover the spec's tables.",
